@startuml
title Archive Search Workbench - sequence: search -> open -> read\n(transparent local read; USB/IP only when needed)

actor User as U
participant "Browser" as B
participant "web_app.py\n(app host :5059)" as APP
database "SQLite\ncatalog" as DB
participant "Per-machine agent\n(your machine :5060)" as AG
participant "Drive" as D

== Search (always works, even offline) ==
U -> B : search term
B -> APP : GET /api/search/metadata
APP -> DB : query
DB --> APP : results (label + path)
APP -> AG : GET /disks  (which drives are connected now?)
AG --> APP : volumes + UUID
APP --> B : results; open enabled only for connected drives

== Open (transparent) ==
U -> B : click "View" on a result
B -> APP : GET /api/smart-serve?label&path
alt Drive mounted on the app host
    APP -> APP : read local file
else Drive attached to your machine
    APP -> AG : GET /read-file?volume=UUID&path (token)
    AG -> D : read file (read-only)
    D --> AG : bytes
    AG --> APP : bytes
else Drive not connected anywhere
    APP --> B : "Connect drive X"  (auto-detect polls until it appears)
end
APP --> B : file (or ZIP for multi-select)
B --> U : file shown / downloaded

== Optional: index a new drive via USB/IP ==
U -> B : attach via USB/IP
B -> APP : POST /api/remote/attach
APP -> AG : POST /bind (busid)
APP -> APP : usbip attach -> /dev/sdX -> mount ro -> scan -> catalog
@enduml
